id: q-space/protocol-coherence-lacunae
title: "Protocol coherence lacunae"
kind: unresolved-question-projection
status: proposed
updated: 2026-08-28

arena: yawn.bot/new.v0.1-conformance
profile_status: working-draft

open_lacunae:
  - id: aggregate-cross-document-resolver
    question: "How will exact Yawn, principal, authority, policy, RoutingProposal, StructuralChangeReceipt, Source, and proof references resolve and fail closed as one aggregate?"
    current_boundary: "Document-local grammar and semantic validators do not prove materialization or application."
  - id: interaction-application-resolver
    question: "How will a consumer authenticate identity, prove current-state CAS, enforce receipt-ID idempotency, and prevent privacy/egress widening before a View transition?"
    current_boundary: "A self-consistent Interaction Operator Receipt is not sufficient application authority."
  - id: lifecycle-supersession-head-chain
    question: "How will corrected ratification, rebinding, pause/reactivation, activation replacement, and retirement preserve one replayable head?"
    current_boundary: "Strict V0.1 requires one binding and permits at most one activation receipt for each objective-steward or worker bot; the root carries no binding, and ambiguous duplicates are rejected."

proof_to_close:
  - versioned schema and reducer
  - authenticated authority and privacy adversaries
  - append-only concurrency and idempotency tests
  - cross-document fixtures with missing, stale, forged, and conflicting refs
  - maintainer-reviewed RFC and migration path

non_claims:
  - "Working-draft profile inclusion is not aggregate resolution."
  - "Local validation is not authority to apply a transition."
  - "A timestamp is not a supersession or atomic-batch identity."
